speechtext:
Tenders were called for; there had to be at least three tenders for any one pasture. These tenders were made by hardware merchants or dealers who sell these supplies. The same thing is true in regard to posts; the posts were purchased by tender and shipped to the railway point nearest to the pasture. The work itself was done under a foreman by the farmers in the locality;

Prairie Farm Rehabilitation
the fences were actually built by the farmers who are going to use that pasture and pay for its maintenance and everything connected with it.
